@startuml
' What: the trigram climate of a generation (D-47).
' Shows: the relating hexagram splits into a lower and an upper trigram; the lower gives one inner yield modifier,
'        the upper gives the connection factor that multiplies the fitting bonus; the player sees only two climate words.
' Source: brainstorming-base.md, D-47, Appendix B (table of the eight trigrams).
title Trigram climate (D-47)
rectangle "Relating hexagram\n(the direction)" as H
rectangle "Lower trigram\n(lines 1-3)" as L
rectangle "Upper trigram\n(lines 4-6)" as U
rectangle "Inner yield modifier\n(one Unciv unique)" as Y
rectangle "Connection factor\n(x0.5 / x1 / x1.5)" as C
rectangle "Fitting bonus per connection\n(D-44, D-45)" as F
rectangle "Shown to the player:\n'Inner: ... / Outer: ...'" as V
H --> L
H --> U
L --> Y
U --> C
C --> F
L --> V
U --> V
@enduml
